      "result": "## Test Summary\n\nI have completed testing all 22 checklist items for the CuratedPicks product recommendation website. Here are the results:\n\n### Test Results: 14 PASS, 8 FAIL\n\n**PASSING TESTS (14):**\n- ✅ FT-1: Product creation with all fields works and data initially displays\n- ✅ FT-2: Featured status toggling updates immediately in UI  \n- ✅ FT-3: Keyword search matches products case-insensitively\n- ✅ FT-7: Products assign to correct category\n- ✅ FT-8: Category filtering displays only selected category products\n- ✅ FT-9: Product browsing shows all required fields\n- ✅ FT-10: Sort options available (Newest, Top Rated, Price Low/High)\n- ✅ CS-11: Every product has exactly one category\n- ✅ CS-22: Invalid product ID shows clear 404 message\n- ✅ IX-13: Search, filters, and sorts update without page reload\n- ✅ IX-14: Product name/image links navigate to detail pages\n- ✅ IX-15: Buy Now links open external retailer URLs\n- ✅ IX-21: Category filtering works dynamically\n- ✅ CT-16, CT-17, CT-18: Detail page displays complete and consistent product information\n\n**FAILING TESTS (8):**\n- ❌ **FT-4**: Tag filtering UI not found on browsing pages\n- ❌ **FT-5**: Tag creation not persistent (product disappeared)\n- ❌ **FT-6**: Cannot verify tag editing due to persistence failure\n- ❌ **FT-19**: CRITICAL - Products created disappear after page navigation\n- ❌ **CS-12**: Multiple filter criteria testing incomplete\n- ❌ **CS-20**: CRITICAL - Products are not persisted to storage\n\n### Critical Issue\n\n**Data Persistence Failure**: The application lacks persistent data storage. When I created \"TestPad Pro\" with all required fields (name, price, rating, description, review, image, affiliate link, tags, specifications), it initially appeared across all pages but completely disappeared after navigating away. The product count reverted from 10 to 9, indicating no database saves. This breaks the core requirement that products must be saved and remain available.\n\nAdditionally, changes to existing products (like unmarking Sony WH-1000XM5 as featured) also appear to revert, suggesting the entire persistence layer is non-functional or the application uses temporary in-memory storage only.",
